# Things Git should ignore.
#
# Aditya: this file keeps junk out of your GitHub repo. Two of these matter
# a lot:
#
#   venv/     — thousands of library files. They'd bloat your repo and anyone
#               can recreate them from requirements.txt in 30 seconds.
#   items.db  — your actual database. Keeping it out means you don't publish
#               real people's names and contact info to the public internet.
#               That's a privacy thing, and it's the kind of judgment call
#               worth mentioning in your submission write-up.

venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

items.db

static/uploads/*
!static/uploads/.gitkeep

.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
scratch.py